From: Try FydeOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] win32: keep UTF-8 paths working with msvcrt

Applies after qemu-sdl-edid-density.patch.

Try Omarchy's 0009 sets the UCRT's LC_CTYPE to UTF-8 and exits when that
fails, because the UCRT converts narrow paths with its own locale. This
runtime is built with Fedora's mingw64 toolchain, which targets msvcrt:
msvcrt has no UTF-8 locale, so the check aborted every start, and it
needs none, since it hands narrow paths to the ANSI Win32 calls, which
use the UTF-8 code page that 0009's manifest selects. Run the check on
the UCRT only.

diff --git a/util/cutils.c b/util/cutils.c
index 5816f8e5..4bdeef8e 100644
--- a/util/cutils.c
+++ b/util/cutils.c
@@ -1056,10 +1056,12 @@ void qemu_init_exec_dir(const char *argv0)
      * This runs before option parsing in both the emulator and qemu-img.
      * Leave numeric parsing and formatting in the C locale.
      */
+#ifdef _UCRT
     if (!setlocale(LC_CTYPE, ".UTF8")) {
         fprintf(stderr, "QEMU requires UTF-8 support in the Windows UCRT\n");
         exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
     }
+#endif
 
     if (exec_dir) {
         return;
